  <!-- ─── CHAINING ─── -->
  <h2 id="chaining">Chaining work</h2>

  <p>Work chains define a dependency graph: each step only runs after its predecessor succeeds. The output <code>Data</code> of one worker is merged and passed as input to the next. Chains support both sequential steps and parallel fan-out/fan-in patterns. If any worker returns <code>Result.failure()</code>, all downstream work is cancelled automatically (unless you override this with <code>setInputMerger</code> or structure the chain differently).</p>

