  <!-- ─── DOZE MODE ─── -->
  <h2 id="doze-mode">Doze mode &amp; App Standby</h2>

  <p>Doze mode is Android&rsquo;s most impactful battery optimisation. Understanding it precisely tells you why certain work runs late or not at all in production, and which APIs actually pierce through it.</p>

  <h3 id="doze-deep">Full Doze vs Light Doze</h3>

  <p>Android distinguishes two levels. <strong>Full Doze</strong> activates when the device is stationary, unplugged, and the screen has been off for an extended period. <strong>Light Doze</strong> (Android 7.0+) activates when the screen is off and the device is unplugged <em>but moving</em> &mdash; like when it&rsquo;s in your pocket. Light Doze applies most of the same restrictions but opens maintenance windows more frequently.</p>

